# doc-check.sh sensitive paths for archiver (archiver#190).
#
# Replaces the shipping-work-python-fastapi defaults wholesale - one path per
# line, `#`-comments and blank lines ignored. Entries match whole path
# SEGMENTS at any depth, so `pyproject.toml` covers clients/python/'s too.
#
# Dropped from the upstream defaults because they match nothing in this tree:
# schema.sql (Alembic owns the schema), src/models/ (models live in src/core/),
# .env.example (env vars are documented in docs/DEPLOYMENT.md, never templated).
# tests/scripts/test_doc_sensitive_paths.py fails on any entry that goes dead.

# Agent + human orientation docs; CLAUDE.md is a symlink to AGENTS.md.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
README.md
CHANGELOG.md

# Dependency surface - docs/DEPLOYMENT.md carries the wheelhouse and resolution story.
pyproject.toml
uv.lock

# The changelog trigger's four paths (AGENTS.md, "Changelog"), plus the domain
# and dashboard trees whose living docs are a CR blocker. `src/` rather than
# src/api/ + src/core/ + src/dashboard/: those three are the whole tree today,
# so enumerating them buys nothing and would leave a future package unwatched -
# the same silent miss the segment-matching fix was about.
alembic/versions/
src/
clients/python/

# Deploy + operator surface. Both entries over-match into the test tree:
# `deploy/` also catches tests/deploy/ (which asserts file parity with deploy/)
# and `scripts/` also catches tests/scripts/. Both land on the same docs anyway.
deploy/
scripts/
